      "text": "**Step 1: Understanding the problem**\nWe are given that when a number \\( n \\) is divided by 6, it leaves a remainder of 1. This means that \\( n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6} \\).\n\n**Step 2: Express \\( n \\) in terms of the remainder**\nSince \\( n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6} \\), we can write \\( n \\) as:\n\\[ n = 6k + 1 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\n**Step 3: Express \\( n + 2010 \\) in terms of the remainder**\nThe problem asks for the remainder when \\( n + 2010 \\) is divided by 6. We can substitute \\( n \\) from the previous step:\n\\[ n + 2010 = (6k + 1) + 2010 = 6k + 2011 \\]\n\n**Step 4: Determine the remainder of \\( n + 2010 \\) when divided by 6**\nWe now find the remainder when \\( 6k + 2011 \\) is divided by 6. Notice that:\n\\[ 6k \\equiv 0 \\pmod{6} \\]\nbecause \\( 6k \\) is a multiple of 6.\n\nThus,\n\\[ 6k + 2011 \\equiv 0 + 1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6} \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( n + 2010 \\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
